Now chromosome fusion,

00:23:02.880 --> 00:23:05.850
where literally a pair of chromosomes

00:23:05.850 --> 00:23:09.690
fuses directly on top of
another pair of chromosomes

00:23:09.690 --> 00:23:11.280
is not totally uncommon.

00:23:11.280 --> 00:23:14.223
It happens at about one in
one 1,000 births, right?

00:23:15.448 --> 00:23:17.950
You can result in some issues sometimes

00:23:17.950 --> 00:23:20.450
but it's not always the case.

00:23:20.450 --> 00:23:23.550
So if apes and humans are closely related

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:25.290
like evolution suggests,

00:23:25.290 --> 00:23:29.020
then it seems that a common
ancestor to both humans and apes

00:23:29.020 --> 00:23:32.010
had his or her chromosomes fused together.

00:23:32.010 --> 00:23:32.870
Okay?

00:23:32.870 --> 00:23:35.480
So all right, do we see this in the DNA?

00:23:35.480 --> 00:23:36.610
Like what do we see in the DNA?

00:23:36.610 --> 00:23:39.530
Well, in humans the second
chromosome appears to be a fusion

00:23:39.530 --> 00:23:42.420
of two great ape chromosomes.

00:23:42.420 --> 00:23:44.720
First, there are two
sections of Chromosome 2

00:23:44.720 --> 00:23:46.200
that correspond directly

00:23:46.200 --> 00:23:49.267
to two separate chromosomes in Apes.

00:23:49.267 --> 00:23:50.640
Let me give an analogy

00:23:50.640 --> 00:23:52.963
if you're having trouble following this.

00:23:53.830 --> 00:23:56.410
DNA is basically an instruction manual

00:23:56.410 --> 00:23:59.890
on how to build something, how
to build an organism right?

00:23:59.890 --> 00:24:01.120
So let's just simplify this

00:24:01.120 --> 00:24:05.786
and just say that this
book is 24 pages long.

00:24:05.786 --> 00:24:09.280
And let's say on page
two are the instructions

00:24:09.280 --> 00:24:11.697
on how to make a hand and on page three

00:24:11.697 --> 00:24:14.310
are the instructions
on how to make a foot.

00:24:14.310 --> 00:24:16.770
And so that's what you see
when you look at a chimpanzee.

00:24:16.770 --> 00:24:18.570
But then when you look at a human,

00:24:18.570 --> 00:24:21.970
you see that it goes from
page two to page four

00:24:21.970 --> 00:24:23.570
and there is no page three.

00:24:23.570 --> 00:24:25.150
But then you look closely at page two

00:24:25.150 --> 00:24:27.780
and realize that it's
page two and page three

00:24:27.780 --> 00:24:29.420
glued on top of each other

00:24:29.420 --> 00:24:31.130
and you see the instructions for the hand

00:24:31.130 --> 00:24:35.690
and the instructions for the
foot on this long page two.

00:24:35.690 --> 00:24:36.560
Does that make sense?

00:24:36.560 --> 00:24:37.393
Yeah.

00:24:37.393 --> 00:24:38.530
That's a simple explanation

00:24:38.530 --> 00:24:40.420
or a simple analogy for
kind of understanding this.

00:24:40.420 --> 00:24:42.674
This is why our feet and
hands are stuck together?

00:24:42.674 --> 00:24:43.747
Exactly.

00:24:43.747 --> 00:24:44.760
And Apes are not.

00:24:44.760 --> 00:24:48.970
Again, this is a grossly
simplified analogy

00:24:48.970 --> 00:24:51.460
but it does help to understand it.

00:24:51.460 --> 00:24:53.610
Now, but furthermore,

00:24:53.610 --> 00:24:55.160
there are these things called telomeres

00:24:55.160 --> 00:24:58.110
at the end of chromosomes

00:24:58.110 --> 00:25:00.810
which basically are these
like redundant material

00:25:00.810 --> 00:25:04.720
that basically protects
the DNA structure, right?

00:25:04.720 --> 00:25:06.060
And so think of it

00:25:06.060 --> 00:25:08.220
like you've got a header
and a footer on a page.

00:25:08.220 --> 00:25:09.053
Right?

00:25:09.053 --> 00:25:09.886
So there's always a header

00:25:09.886 --> 00:25:11.060
and there's always a footer on a page

00:25:11.060 --> 00:25:13.970
and if you were to take two
pages and glue them together,

00:25:13.970 --> 00:25:16.160
in the middle of those two pages,

00:25:16.160 --> 00:25:19.140
there would be a header and a
footer glued together, right?

00:25:19.140 --> 00:25:21.440
If you take two pages and you
glue them on top of each other

00:25:21.440 --> 00:25:23.260
like a really long page,

00:25:23.260 --> 00:25:24.093
Yeah.

00:25:24.093 --> 00:25:26.430
A header and footer would
be touching each other.

00:25:26.430 --> 00:25:31.170
Well, we see two telomeres,
two vestigial telomeres

00:25:32.020 --> 00:25:33.910
directly on top of each other

00:25:33.910 --> 00:25:37.730
in the middle of the
second chromosome, right?

00:25:37.730 --> 00:25:41.310
So all the evidence is pointing
