00:47:07.557 --> 00:47:10.510
I tried living like this.

00:47:10.510 --> 00:47:12.883
I ran into a few problems.

00:47:12.883 --> 00:47:17.883
The music did not continue to
resonate well in your bosom?

00:47:17.950 --> 00:47:21.620
Basically, the foundation
of my faith ultimately

00:47:21.620 --> 00:47:23.560
was still the Bible even if I had sort of

00:47:23.560 --> 00:47:27.390
a more liberal view or more gray view

00:47:27.390 --> 00:47:29.980
of what the Bible might
mean and represent.

00:47:29.980 --> 00:47:33.550
And so every time I read the
Bible, I saw issues with it.

00:47:33.550 --> 00:47:36.560
Every time I heard a sermon,
I would have an issue with it.

00:47:36.560 --> 00:47:40.350
My experience through Christianity
was basically inflaming

00:47:40.350 --> 00:47:42.030
my doubts and my questions.

00:47:42.030 --> 00:47:44.190
So the closer I got to it,

00:47:44.190 --> 00:47:48.220
the more I couldn't quite
shake these questions

00:47:48.220 --> 00:47:49.290
that continue to linger.

00:47:49.290 --> 00:47:52.124
And the question, the
place that I had sort of

00:47:52.124 --> 00:47:55.279
put a barrier around and
said we're not going there

00:47:55.279 --> 00:47:57.530
sure we can talk about evolution,

00:47:57.530 --> 00:48:00.230
we can talk about the
historicity of the Old Testament

00:48:01.070 --> 00:48:03.930
but where I'm not gonna go
is I'm not gonna go to Jesus.

00:48:03.930 --> 00:48:06.010
I'm not gonna question Jesus.

00:48:06.010 --> 00:48:08.950
But I just couldn't help myself

00:48:08.950 --> 00:48:12.380
because I was like my
understanding of who Jesus is

00:48:12.380 --> 00:48:14.740
is not just based on my
experience with him personally

00:48:14.740 --> 00:48:17.500
but it's also based on what
the Bible has to say about him.

00:48:17.500 --> 00:48:20.965
This is how we know what
there is to know about Jesus.

00:48:20.965 --> 00:48:24.730
And again, when I looked into this

00:48:24.730 --> 00:48:27.023
my world was rocked in a very big way.

00:48:28.031 --> 00:48:30.746
I'm not gonna give sufficient detail here.

00:48:30.746 --> 00:48:32.980
Lots of people have gone and done this

00:48:32.980 --> 00:48:35.050
who are smarter and more educated than me.

00:48:35.050 --> 00:48:38.130
But basically, there are
just as many views on this

00:48:38.130 --> 00:48:40.040
as there are people who study it.

00:48:40.040 --> 00:48:43.760
But essentially, I live
my whole life being sure

00:48:43.760 --> 00:48:46.030
that the Gospels were
historically reliable,

00:48:46.030 --> 00:48:47.160
almost taking it for granted.

00:48:47.160 --> 00:48:48.367
I mean I'd read Josh McDowell's

00:48:48.367 --> 00:48:49.680
"Evidence That Demands a Verdict"

00:48:49.680 --> 00:48:53.030
and Josh McDowell "New Evidence
That Demands a Verdict".

00:48:53.030 --> 00:48:55.920
I had read Lee Strobel's
"Case for Christ".

00:48:55.920 --> 00:48:58.840
I could spit these arguments
back out to you on an airplane

00:48:58.840 --> 00:49:01.440
and make you think that
well, I must be a Christian.

00:49:02.431 --> 00:49:04.670
Why on an airplane by the way?

00:49:04.670 --> 00:49:07.360
Because when you're evangelical Christian

00:49:07.360 --> 00:49:08.430
you sit next to a stranger,

00:49:08.430 --> 00:49:10.440
this may be the only
opportunity you ever have

00:49:10.440 --> 00:49:12.950
to share the life-changing
message of Jesus with them.

00:49:12.950 --> 00:49:15.120
There were lots of conversations

00:49:15.120 --> 00:49:17.201
that involved airplane evangelism

00:49:17.201 --> 00:49:19.590
because it was just like
his captive audience.

00:49:19.590 --> 00:49:20.423
Yeah.

00:49:20.423 --> 00:49:21.710
It's like you're gonna
go this whole flight

00:49:21.710 --> 00:49:22.543
and not saying anything.

00:49:22.543 --> 00:49:23.830
Right, what if it crashes?

00:49:24.927 --> 00:49:28.970
But I took a second to go one layer deeper

00:49:28.970 --> 00:49:32.290
and to look at the answers
to the Christian answers

00:49:32.290 --> 00:49:34.260
that I had been given all my life.

00:49:34.260 --> 00:49:36.400
And that was when I realized
that this Jesus thing

00:49:36.400 --> 00:49:40.973
was very, very messy from
a historical standpoint.

00:49:42.400 --> 00:49:43.720
There's a few books that do a good job

00:49:43.720 --> 00:49:45.890
of outlining some of this stuff.

00:49:45.890 --> 00:49:49.140
One of them is "Jesus
Interrupted" by Bart Ehrman

00:49:49.140 --> 00:49:51.240
who's a professor of New Testament at UNC

00:49:51.240 --> 00:49:53.550
who incidentally Jessie was in his class

00:49:53.550 --> 00:49:55.180
and she used to come home every single day

00:49:55.180 --> 00:49:56.700
and then we would come up with ways

00:49:56.700 --> 00:49:59.053
to go back to argue
against him, ironically.

00:50:00.230 --> 00:50:01.890
Me and you were actually involved

00:50:01.890 --> 00:50:05.690
in a Campus Crusade initiative
on the campus of UNC

00:50:05.690 --> 00:50:07.910
to kind of combat what he was doing

00:50:07.910 --> 00:50:10.840
because he was having so much
influence on the students.

00:50:10.840 --> 00:50:14.210
So I understood Bart Ehrman
had been the enemy for so long

00:50:14.210 --> 00:50:15.270
but what I started to realize

00:50:15.270 --> 00:50:17.090
is that he had a very similar story

00:50:17.090 --> 00:50:19.320
and I thought that he dealt
with the subject matter

00:50:19.320 --> 00:50:21.440
in an honest and even-handed way.

00:50:21.440 --> 00:50:22.447
There's also a book called

00:50:22.447 --> 00:50:24.960
"The Historical Jesus: Five Views"

00:50:24.960 --> 00:50:27.007
which kind of runs the spectrum once again

00:50:27.007 --> 00:50:29.490
on how you can see this.

00:50:29.490 --> 00:50:31.740
But basically what I just saw is that

00:50:31.740 --> 00:50:33.420
there's so many people coming at this

00:50:33.420 --> 00:50:36.230
with an intention to uncover the truth,

00:50:36.230 --> 00:50:37.480
to find the truth

00:50:37.480 --> 00:50:39.510
and they're coming to these
wildly different conclusions.

00:50:39.510 --> 00:50:41.540
This isn't like science.

00:50:41.540 --> 00:50:44.793
Somebody does a scientific
experiment in 1985 in China

00:50:44.793 --> 00:50:47.120
and then somebody does the
same scientific experiment

00:50:47.120 --> 00:50:49.785
in 2019 in California.

00:50:49.785 --> 00:50:51.280
If everything is controlled,

00:50:51.280 --> 00:50:53.100
they're gonna come to the same conclusion.

00:50:53.100 --> 00:50:54.980
That's not how history works

00:50:54.980 --> 00:50:57.040
and it makes it very difficult

00:50:57.040 --> 00:50:59.090
to come to definitive
conclusions about things.

00:50:59.090 --> 00:51:03.570
But essentially in the end,
by far to me personally,

00:51:03.570 --> 00:51:06.900
the most compelling and
seemingly reasonable view

00:51:06.900 --> 00:51:08.770
was that the Gospels appear

00:51:08.770 --> 00:51:10.720
to be a mix of religious propaganda

00:51:10.720 --> 00:51:12.300
as well as actual history.

00:51:12.300 --> 00:51:14.420
So there's definitely
some history in there.

00:51:14.420 --> 00:51:17.250
I think Jesus was a real
person, so does Bart Ehrman.

00:51:17.250 --> 00:51:19.748
But I don't think that
as he is presented there

00:51:19.748 --> 00:51:21.773
is completely reliable.

00:51:22.920 --> 00:51:24.380
That's what I was thinking at the time.

00:51:24.380 --> 00:51:26.740
So what did you believe about Jesus?

00:51:26.740 --> 00:51:29.922
You reached a conclusion
about the person of Jesus

00:51:29.922 --> 00:51:34.210
at that time when you were
when you're researching that.

00:51:34.210 --> 00:51:36.580
I had a picture of Jesus

00:51:36.580 --> 00:51:38.960
that was the picture that I had always had

00:51:39.800 --> 00:51:42.620
of this person who did these miracles

00:51:42.620 --> 00:51:44.540
and died on the cross and rose again

00:51:44.540 --> 00:51:47.570
and died for my sins and
was God in the flesh.

00:51:47.570 --> 00:51:50.600
All the things that were
important to believe about him.

00:51:50.600 --> 00:51:53.430
But I had doubts about
those things being true

00:51:53.430 --> 00:51:55.720
but I didn't have
another picture of Jesus.

00:51:55.720 --> 00:51:57.270
There was no other picture of Jesus.

00:51:57.270 --> 00:51:58.103
So you read all these books,

00:51:58.103 --> 00:51:59.500
you did all this research about Jesus

00:51:59.500 --> 00:52:01.060
but your conclusion was

00:52:01.955 --> 00:52:04.620
not really a conclusion at that point?

00:52:04.620 --> 00:52:05.810
Oh yeah, it was some process.

00:52:05.810 --> 00:52:08.955
and so this was incredibly
unsettling, right?

00:52:08.955 --> 00:52:12.320
This was way more unsettling

00:52:12.320 --> 00:52:14.150
than anything that had happened so far

00:52:14.150 --> 00:52:16.680
because this was Jesus, this
was the core of everything.

00:52:16.680 --> 00:52:18.290
This is who my relationship was with

00:52:18.290 --> 00:52:19.160
and all of a sudden,

00:52:19.160 --> 00:52:22.930
I've got very serious doubts about him.

00:52:22.930 --> 00:52:24.830
And I think that anyone

00:52:24.830 --> 00:52:28.135
that you would have conversations with

00:52:28.135 --> 00:52:31.140
and you did initiate with not only Jesse

00:52:31.140 --> 00:52:34.520
but with me and with other people

00:52:34.520 --> 00:52:38.421
that you confided in over this decade

00:52:38.421 --> 00:52:40.173
of going through this.

00:52:41.759 --> 00:52:43.880
If you were talking to someone

00:52:43.880 --> 00:52:48.880
who was it was still very
much committed to their faith,

00:52:48.930 --> 00:52:51.210
it was like much more solid,

00:52:51.210 --> 00:52:53.670
I think the response maybe it's not spoken

00:52:53.670 --> 00:52:58.237
is well yeah, as long as you
as long as you hold on to Jesus

00:52:58.237 --> 00:52:59.470
and you know it's like that,

00:52:59.470 --> 00:53:00.303
you can't let go of that.

00:53:00.303 --> 00:53:01.860
You can let go everything else

00:53:01.860 --> 00:53:06.860
but you can't really let go of
what you believe about Jesus

00:53:07.043 --> 00:53:08.777
raising from the dead and

00:53:08.777 --> 00:53:12.720
and paying the penalty for
your sins instead of you.

00:53:12.720 --> 00:53:13.553
Yeah.

00:53:13.553 --> 00:53:15.420
Either you go to hell or or he does

00:53:15.420 --> 00:53:16.371
which he already did and came back.

00:53:16.371 --> 00:53:17.980
Right
Is the belief.

00:53:17.980 --> 00:53:22.980
So you can let other stuff
go and maybe not panic

00:53:24.190 --> 00:53:26.790
and again I'll share my perspective

00:53:26.790 --> 00:53:29.040
on interacting with you more next week

00:53:29.040 --> 00:53:31.363
but at times, that was part of it.

00:53:32.210 --> 00:53:36.390
Yeah because what you believe
about Jesus is paramount

00:53:36.390 --> 00:53:38.190
but what you believe about Jesus

00:53:38.190 --> 00:53:40.520
is still based on what is
presented in the Bible.

00:53:40.520 --> 00:53:42.150
If not, where else are you getting it?

00:53:42.150 --> 00:53:43.070
I mean some people might be like

00:53:43.070 --> 00:53:45.262
well I'm getting it directly from God

00:53:45.262 --> 00:53:48.600
but that's not what Christianity teaches.

00:53:48.600 --> 00:53:50.780
It's coming from God and the Bible

00:53:50.780 --> 00:53:52.680
and they don't contradict one another.

00:53:53.750 --> 00:53:55.550
So when it became clear to me

00:53:55.550 --> 00:53:57.540
that it wasn't something
that I could have,

00:53:57.540 --> 00:53:59.853
the same kind of faith
in it that I've had,

00:54:01.000 --> 00:54:03.720
I had a meltdown.

00:54:03.720 --> 00:54:06.320
I didn't do anything crazy externally

00:54:06.320 --> 00:54:08.680
but there was a lot happening internally.

00:54:08.680 --> 00:54:09.513
At this point I said--

00:54:09.513 --> 00:54:10.880
Do you remember a time

00:54:10.880 --> 00:54:13.800
or a place associated with this?

00:54:13.800 --> 00:54:14.790
Well I've got a couple of journal entry

00:54:14.790 --> 00:54:16.380
in another journal entry that I'd go into

00:54:16.380 --> 00:54:18.610
which is sort of the
next stage of this thing

00:54:18.610 --> 00:54:21.300
but not particularly.

00:54:21.300 --> 00:54:23.720
But I do remember saying this at the time.

00:54:23.720 --> 00:54:28.392
I was like "God you are
bigger than all of this right.

00:54:28.392 --> 00:54:31.327
"I'm just this little human

00:54:31.327 --> 00:54:33.547
"who sees through a glass darkly my

00:54:33.547 --> 00:54:36.987
"I got this finite mind and
I'm trying to understand

00:54:36.987 --> 00:54:40.060
"the infinite mind, the
creator of the universe."

00:54:40.060 --> 00:54:43.030
Seems pretty arrogant actually you know.

00:54:43.030 --> 00:54:45.248
And I was like is God just sitting there

00:54:45.248 --> 00:54:47.160
watching me do all this research

00:54:47.160 --> 00:54:49.890
and eventually he's gonna
give me some satisfying answer

00:54:49.890 --> 00:54:51.170
and then all I said I'm gonna have faith.

00:54:51.170 --> 00:54:53.450
That just doesn't seem
like a relationship.

00:54:53.450 --> 00:54:55.120
That's not how you conduct a relationship.

00:54:55.120 --> 00:54:58.170
I don't make my wife
fit a certain criteria.

00:54:58.170 --> 00:55:02.122
I don't ask her a bunch of
questions about her past

00:55:02.122 --> 00:55:04.767
in order for her to qualify
to be you know I'm saying?

00:55:04.767 --> 00:55:07.459
it's like I experience
relationship with her

00:55:07.459 --> 00:55:09.680
on a personal level

00:55:09.680 --> 00:55:13.320
and I just felt like I was
just completely in my mind

00:55:13.320 --> 00:55:15.746
and I made this whole thing
like scientific and intellectual

00:55:15.746 --> 00:55:19.020
and also it seemed like
I was being arrogant

00:55:19.020 --> 00:55:22.972
because I was waiting for
God to fit my expectations.

00:55:22.972 --> 00:55:26.190
I was creating God in my own image

00:55:26.190 --> 00:55:29.130
as opposed to creating me in His image.

00:55:29.130 --> 00:55:30.790
I had flipped the script on God

00:55:30.790 --> 00:55:33.290
and was waiting for him to
like be my little trick pony

00:55:33.290 --> 00:55:34.910
that does all the things
that I want him to do

00:55:34.910 --> 00:55:37.370
in order for me to believe in him.

00:55:37.370 --> 00:55:38.450
There's a verse that kind of gets in.

00:55:38.450 --> 00:55:40.210
Which was answers basically.

00:55:40.210 --> 00:55:45.137
Isaiah 55 says "For my
thoughts are not your thoughts,

00:55:45.137 --> 00:55:48.337
"neither are your ways my
ways, declares the Lord.

00:55:48.337 --> 00:55:50.187
"As the heavens are higher than the earth

00:55:50.187 --> 00:55:52.307
"So are my ways higher than your ways

00:55:52.307 --> 00:55:54.477
"and my thoughts than your thoughts".

00:55:55.640 --> 00:55:58.290
So God saying I'm bigger than you.

00:55:58.290 --> 00:55:59.123
Right.

00:55:59.123 --> 00:56:02.700
There's certain things
you just can't get, dude.

00:56:02.700 --> 00:56:05.930
Yeah and at this point, I was like okay

00:56:05.930 --> 00:56:10.181
you know what, I think this is
probably where faith comes in

00:56:10.181 --> 00:56:13.680
It makes sense to me that this
might be where faith comes in

00:56:13.680 --> 00:56:18.680
because I am sitting here
trying to prove this stuff out

00:56:21.166 --> 00:56:24.040
but shouldn't I just have faith first

00:56:24.040 --> 00:56:27.820
and then maybe these answers
will be given to me by God.

00:56:27.820 --> 00:56:29.260
Isn't this what faith is all about?

00:56:29.260 --> 00:56:30.320
I mean the whole point is this.

00:56:30.320 --> 00:56:33.800
It's evidence of things not seen, right?

00:56:33.800 --> 00:56:37.340
And so your next step was
there's no way for me to know

00:56:37.340 --> 00:56:38.760
but I'm gonna try a different route

00:56:38.760 --> 00:56:41.956
which is I'm gonna maybe
faith needs to come first.

00:56:41.956 --> 00:56:42.789
Yeah

00:56:42.789 --> 00:56:44.680
And would then we'll open up,

00:56:44.680 --> 00:56:46.090
maybe that'll lead to something.

00:56:46.090 --> 00:56:49.920
Yeah, I can believe in the
Jesus that I believe in

00:56:49.920 --> 00:56:51.510
because that's what the Bible says.

00:56:51.510 --> 00:56:53.450
I can believe in the biblical Jesus

00:56:53.450 --> 00:56:56.600
even though I have reasons that
from historical perspective

00:56:56.600 --> 00:56:58.220
to doubt that I can still believe in it

00:56:58.220 --> 00:56:59.820
and overcome that.

00:56:59.820 --> 00:57:02.580
And this is when I ran into some problems.

00:57:02.580 --> 00:57:06.860
So the first thing was how
does this differentiate me

00:57:06.860 --> 00:57:09.110
from any other faith on earth right?

00:57:09.110 --> 00:57:11.743
One of the things that
makes Christianity a unique

00:57:11.743 --> 00:57:16.743
is that you know it is the
way, the truth and the life.

00:57:18.940 --> 00:57:22.460
No man comes to the Father
except through the son right?

00:57:22.460 --> 00:57:25.290
You don't get to the son
through somebody else.

00:57:25.290 --> 00:57:27.943
You don't get to the Son
through Buddha, right?

00:57:29.181 --> 00:57:33.590
But also evangelical Christians

00:57:33.590 --> 00:57:37.025
tend to be pretty
critical of other faiths.

00:57:37.025 --> 00:57:40.714
Mormonism is a perfect example right?

00:57:40.714 --> 00:57:42.720
If you're in an evangelical church

00:57:42.720 --> 00:57:45.300
or certain evangelical churches you know,

00:57:45.300 --> 00:57:49.130
they teach you that Mormons
basically have it wrong,

00:57:49.130 --> 00:57:54.130
that Mormonism is a bastardization
of Christianity, right.

00:57:55.157 --> 00:57:58.206
It's not just another Christian group

00:57:58.206 --> 00:58:01.530
and they lots of
Christians will write books

00:58:01.530 --> 00:58:03.720
that explain how all the things

00:58:03.720 --> 00:58:05.750
that Mormons believe about Joseph Smith

00:58:05.750 --> 00:58:07.990
and these things that
happened are not true

00:58:07.990 --> 00:58:10.090
and here's why in the
Book of Mormon is not true

00:58:10.090 --> 00:58:11.420
and here's why.

00:58:11.420 --> 00:58:13.703
So they can be very
critical of that faith.

00:58:15.190 --> 00:58:19.553
But yet, if you say
those things to a Mormon,

00:58:19.553 --> 00:58:24.553
they will say well, I have
a burning in the bosom

00:58:24.636 --> 00:58:28.160
that proves to me that
these things are right.

00:58:28.160 --> 00:58:30.460
So you can tell me that
these things seem wrong

00:58:30.460 --> 00:58:32.750
and you can show me certain things

00:58:32.750 --> 00:58:36.490
but I believe them to be true
and you can't change that

00:58:36.490 --> 00:58:41.490
because I have this sort
of seal and sign from God,

00:58:41.660 --> 00:58:43.950
this indication that this faith is real

00:58:43.950 --> 00:58:45.500
and this is all true.

00:58:45.500 --> 00:58:50.500
And I was like, isn't that
what I'm doing right now?

00:58:52.210 --> 00:58:54.090
Now I'm just saying that
I'm just gonna have faith

00:58:54.090 --> 00:58:55.640
that things are real.

00:58:55.640 --> 00:58:57.113
Damn the evidence.

00:58:58.410 --> 00:59:00.660
So how does that make
me any different right?

00:59:01.680 --> 00:59:03.400
And ultimately, this kind of faith

00:59:03.400 --> 00:59:05.870
felt a little cowardly
to me, to be honest.

00:59:05.870 --> 00:59:08.406
It felt like what I was saying is yeah,

00:59:08.406 --> 00:59:10.050
there's some conclusions

00:59:10.050 --> 00:59:11.660
that I really don't wanna come to

00:59:11.660 --> 00:59:13.960
and the way I'm going to avoid those

00:59:13.960 --> 00:59:15.550
is just by having faith.

00:59:15.550 --> 00:59:18.040
But ultimately, you just
can't make yourself believe.

00:59:18.040 --> 00:59:20.579
You just can't make yourself have faith.

00:59:20.579 --> 00:59:24.167
This was a torturous place for me, right

00:59:24.167 --> 00:59:26.110
and I was there for a very long time.

00:59:26.110 --> 00:59:27.360
There was lots of praying,

00:59:27.360 --> 00:59:29.010
there was lots of reading the Bible

00:59:29.010 --> 00:59:31.300
which would inflame
some of the same doubts.

00:59:31.300 --> 00:59:33.550
There was lots of talking
to Christians openly

00:59:33.550 --> 00:59:34.550
about what was happening.

00:59:34.550 --> 00:59:37.510
I wanna be very clear that I
didn't go into a cave somewhere

00:59:37.510 --> 00:59:40.541
and come to these conclusions
and never run them by.

00:59:40.541 --> 00:59:43.920
I didn't wanna leave this thing man.

00:59:43.920 --> 00:59:45.291
This was my life.

00:59:45.291 --> 00:59:47.550
This was this defined everything for me.

00:59:47.550 --> 00:59:49.960
This was the foundation of my marriage,

00:59:49.960 --> 00:59:52.050
this was the foundation the
way I was raising my kids.

00:59:52.050 --> 00:59:54.540
I didn't want it to go away.

00:59:54.540 --> 00:59:57.670
It was the orienting
purpose-driven worldview

00:59:57.670 --> 01:00:02.450
that was what was basically
defined everything about me.

01:00:02.450 --> 01:00:07.070
But yet, I'm going through this process.

01:00:07.070 --> 01:00:08.320
I'm talking with people,

01:00:08.320 --> 01:00:10.253
I'm talking to my wife, she's crying.

01:00:11.600 --> 01:00:12.433
You're talking to me.

01:00:12.433 --> 01:00:13.390
Yeah, I'm talking to you.

01:00:13.390 --> 01:00:15.600
I was talking to you the
entire time about this stuff.

01:00:15.600 --> 01:00:16.960
You didn't cry, thank you.

01:00:16.960 --> 01:00:17.793
I didn't cry.

01:00:19.140 --> 01:00:23.077
But the major shift for me occurred

01:00:23.077 --> 01:00:27.100
when I asked a question I had never asked.

01:00:27.100 --> 01:00:28.840
I'd been very very afraid
to ask this question

01:00:28.840 --> 01:00:32.593
and that was what if I'm wrong?

01:00:35.010 --> 01:00:38.120
What if I opened myself
up to the possibility

01:00:38.120 --> 01:00:41.343
that maybe I have been wrong about this?

01:00:43.881 --> 01:00:45.980
I wanna be clear, I'd never done that

01:00:45.980 --> 01:00:49.733
even and all these things
that had like shaken me right.

01:00:50.726 --> 01:00:53.880
all these doubts that I
had, I still was sort of,

01:00:53.880 --> 01:00:57.040
there was this Christian core

01:00:57.980 --> 01:01:01.000
that was completely
protected through all this

01:01:01.000 --> 01:01:02.993
that I wasn't willing to let go of.

01:01:04.640 --> 01:01:07.700
But I was like what if I am wrong?

01:01:07.700 --> 01:01:09.780
Can I just live like
that for a little bit?

01:01:09.780 --> 01:01:11.280
I'm pretty good at kind of giving myself

01:01:11.280 --> 01:01:12.113
over to things, right?

01:01:12.113 --> 01:01:14.580
I can watch a movie and get lost in it.

01:01:14.580 --> 01:01:16.930
I can read a book, I can get lost in it.

01:01:16.930 --> 01:01:18.500
I can read a book from
a different perspective

01:01:18.500 --> 01:01:20.470
and I can adopt that
perspective for a little bit

01:01:20.470 --> 01:01:21.510
to see what it feels like

01:01:21.510 --> 01:01:23.930
and I decided that I was gonna do that.

01:01:23.930 --> 01:01:28.200
So let's just consider what it
would mean if you were wrong.

01:01:28.200 --> 01:01:30.530
What would that mean about the Bible?

01:01:30.530 --> 01:01:32.323
And when I was honest with myself,

01:01:33.380 --> 01:01:36.100
the Bible began to make a lot
more sense to me personally

01:01:36.100 --> 01:01:38.760
as a product of humans rather than God.

01:01:38.760 --> 01:01:42.541
It seemed less and less
like God's message to people

01:01:42.541 --> 01:01:46.610
and more like people's
best guesses about God.

01:01:46.610 --> 01:01:49.883
And in that, it became a lot
like any other holy text.

01:01:52.210 --> 01:01:55.537
And that when I came to
that conclusion, or I was

01:01:55.537 --> 01:01:57.940
and I wasn't fully there
I was just considering

01:01:57.940 --> 01:02:00.023
what does it feel like to think this?

01:02:01.030 --> 01:02:02.820
It led to a few more questions

01:02:02.820 --> 01:02:04.920
that I'd always been afraid to ask myself.

01:02:06.126 --> 01:02:08.760
I'm gonna read these
'cause I wrote them down.

01:02:08.760 --> 01:02:12.177
These are just a few of the
questions I'd always avoided.

01:02:12.177 --> 01:02:13.527
"If I don't have to believe

01:02:13.527 --> 01:02:15.497
"that God ordered his chosen people

01:02:15.497 --> 01:02:18.837
"to slaughter men, women and
children by the thousands,

01:02:18.837 --> 01:02:20.003
"then why would I?

01:02:22.567 --> 01:02:27.567
"If I don't wanna believe that
every religious experience

01:02:27.777 --> 01:02:29.417
"of any person who is not a Christian

01:02:29.417 --> 01:02:33.667
"is ultimately illegitimate,
then why would I?

01:02:33.667 --> 01:02:35.917
"If I don't have to believe that anyone

01:02:35.917 --> 01:02:37.925
"who doesn't have a
relationship with Jesus i.e.

01:02:37.925 --> 01:02:41.097
"the majority of people
who have ever lived

01:02:41.097 --> 01:02:43.157
"are going to spend eternity

01:02:43.157 --> 01:02:45.847
"being literally tortured in a fire

01:02:45.847 --> 01:02:48.497
"experiencing never-ending
pain and suffering

01:02:48.497 --> 01:02:50.107
"then why, no pun intended,

01:02:50.107 --> 01:02:52.393
"in the hell would I believe that?

01:02:53.787 --> 01:02:58.147
"And if I can somehow accept the idea

01:02:58.147 --> 01:03:00.697
"that hell exists
because of God's holiness

01:03:00.697 --> 01:03:02.157
"why would I believe in a God

01:03:02.157 --> 01:03:03.704
"who would choose to create
that particular world

01:03:03.704 --> 01:03:05.817
"where people have no
choice whether or not

01:03:05.817 --> 01:03:08.077
"they're going to be born
but then once they are born,

01:03:08.077 --> 01:03:09.997
"if they don't adopt the
correct understanding of God,

01:03:09.997 --> 01:03:11.997
"he will punish them forever.

01:03:11.997 --> 01:03:14.277
"Why believe in that
God if I don't have to?"

01:03:17.980 --> 01:03:19.330
So where did this leave me?

01:03:20.790 --> 01:03:22.220
Because the answer to those questions

01:03:22.220 --> 01:03:27.110
are that you have, there's a lot of fear

01:03:27.110 --> 01:03:30.410
of what you might lose or experience?

01:03:30.410 --> 01:03:33.865
But there are some things to gain um

01:03:33.865 --> 01:03:37.513
if you go to the other side.

01:03:38.950 --> 01:03:39.783
Well, it's funny because

01:03:39.783 --> 01:03:42.177
I had spent a lot of time in my head,

01:03:42.177 --> 01:03:46.610
a bunch of light intellectual processing

01:03:46.610 --> 01:03:49.883
of all these things right,
philosophical stuff.

01:03:51.130 --> 01:03:52.730
But at this point, as I felt

01:03:52.730 --> 01:03:56.120
this sort of traditional
faith slipping away,

01:03:56.120 --> 01:03:59.000
I started worrying about
some pretty practical things

01:03:59.000 --> 01:04:02.113
like how is my marriage
gonna stay together,

01:04:03.780 --> 01:04:06.300
what am I gonna teach my kids?

01:04:06.300 --> 01:04:08.070
This is what I've been teaching them.

01:04:08.070 --> 01:04:09.620
What am I gonna teach them now?

01:04:11.496 --> 01:04:14.750
What am I gonna do, where am I gonna turn?

01:04:14.750 --> 01:04:16.810
What's gonna replace this?

01:04:16.810 --> 01:04:20.137
This is community, this is purpose,

01:04:20.137 --> 01:04:24.540
this is meaning, where am I
gonna find something like that?

01:04:24.540 --> 01:04:27.630
And a verse came to mind.

01:04:27.630 --> 01:04:30.050
John 6 after Jesus has kind of talked

01:04:30.050 --> 01:04:32.900
about him being the flesh

01:04:32.900 --> 01:04:34.710
and he's kind of basically given

01:04:34.710 --> 01:04:39.710
the whole idea of you know,
communion at this point

01:04:40.090 --> 01:04:45.030
and it's a difficult teaching
and a lot of people walk away

01:04:45.030 --> 01:04:47.250
'cause they're like he's
talking about eating him

01:04:47.250 --> 01:04:48.300
and drinking his blood.

01:04:48.300 --> 01:04:50.580
This dude's nuts and it
was a difficult teaching.

01:04:50.580 --> 01:04:51.890
People didn't understand
what he was getting at

01:04:51.890 --> 01:04:53.150
and they walked away.

01:04:53.150 --> 01:04:55.079
So Jesus asked the twelve?

01:04:55.079 --> 01:04:56.633
Do you wanna leave too?

01:04:58.470 --> 01:05:02.497
Simon Peter replied "Lord
to whom would we go?

01:05:02.497 --> 01:05:04.247
"You have the words of eternal life,

01:05:04.247 --> 01:05:07.767
"we believe and know that
you are the Holy One of God."

01:05:10.066 --> 01:05:11.730
And that's what I said.

01:05:11.730 --> 01:05:14.923
I was like listen, I
got nowhere else to go.

01:05:15.950 --> 01:05:18.293
What am I gonna become?

01:05:20.200 --> 01:05:22.340
Now, let me make it clear.

01:05:22.340 --> 01:05:24.770
I was in a state of panic at this point

01:05:24.770 --> 01:05:27.110
but I was like I can't, I
can't, I can't let this,

01:05:27.110 --> 01:05:28.408
I can't let this go,

01:05:28.408 --> 01:05:32.233
there's too much wrapped
up in this, right?

01:05:33.140 --> 01:05:37.650
But this is where being in Los Angeles

01:05:37.650 --> 01:05:40.350
did allow me to ask a different question.

01:05:40.350 --> 01:05:42.090
And let me let me explain that.

01:05:42.090 --> 01:05:46.440
First of all, I have no
doubt that many people

01:05:46.440 --> 01:05:49.490
will probably not even
listen to this story.

01:05:49.490 --> 01:05:50.760
In fact, I've seen it on Twitter.

01:05:50.760 --> 01:05:53.220
I've already seen people say you know

01:05:53.220 --> 01:05:55.180
I don't wanna listen to
their personal stories

01:05:55.180 --> 01:05:59.040
because I don't wanna hear
somebody talk about leaving

01:05:59.040 --> 01:05:59.873
which that hurts mean that

01:05:59.873 --> 01:06:01.497
you don't wanna listen to the story.

01:06:01.497 --> 01:06:02.620
I'm just trying to be honest

01:06:02.620 --> 01:06:06.150
but I know a lot of people will come

01:06:06.150 --> 01:06:08.340
to the very very easy conclusion.

01:06:08.340 --> 01:06:10.830
Guys, there's nothing
surprising about this.

01:06:10.830 --> 01:06:13.820
You were Christians and
then you went to Los Angeles

01:06:13.820 --> 01:06:15.530
and you lost your faith.

01:06:15.530 --> 01:06:17.475
It's a story as old as Los Angeles.

01:06:19.940 --> 01:06:23.140
This isn't surprising, it's
like what's the big deal?

01:06:23.140 --> 01:06:27.370
This is super simple but
I'm trying to represent

01:06:27.370 --> 01:06:30.030
that this wasn't this
wasn't something made,

01:06:30.030 --> 01:06:31.740
this wasn't some flippant decision,

01:06:31.740 --> 01:06:33.360
this wasn't like ah, man

01:06:33.360 --> 01:06:36.060
I wanna be cool and
accepted in modern culture

01:06:36.060 --> 01:06:37.620
so I'm gonna shed all this stuff.

01:06:37.620 --> 01:06:39.660
The reason why it hurts is because--

01:06:39.660 --> 01:06:40.493
It's a dismissal.

01:06:40.493 --> 01:06:42.944
That assumption is a dismissal,

01:06:42.944 --> 01:06:46.390
it's an assumption of
your of your true motives

01:06:46.390 --> 01:06:47.660
that you don't wanna state

01:06:47.660 --> 01:06:50.811
which are hey you just
wanna sow your wild oats

01:06:50.811 --> 01:06:54.670
or you wanna be cool or you wanna be able

01:06:54.670 --> 01:06:57.660
to face your friends who
believe different things

01:06:57.660 --> 01:06:59.430
or like they have different lifestyles.

01:06:59.430 --> 01:07:02.220
And in order to be successful out there,

01:07:02.220 --> 01:07:04.837
you gotta make some changes, okay.

01:07:04.837 --> 01:07:08.680
I mean watch any award show now

01:07:08.680 --> 01:07:13.560
and see how the entertainment
industry is pushing change

01:07:13.560 --> 01:07:18.560
in perspectives and changes
in the way people act.

01:07:18.620 --> 01:07:20.710
if not belief.

01:07:20.710 --> 01:07:25.550
And so it's like, hey if I get it,

01:07:25.550 --> 01:07:26.680
if you guys wanna go out there

01:07:26.680 --> 01:07:28.010
and you wanna pursue your dreams,

01:07:28.010 --> 01:07:30.510
if that's really what's
most important to you

01:07:30.510 --> 01:07:33.910
then yeah, you got to give up,

01:07:33.910 --> 01:07:36.370
you got to give up your beliefs.

01:07:36.370 --> 01:07:37.830
I mean you gotta make a choice

01:07:37.830 --> 01:07:40.190
and it seems like that's the easy thing.

01:07:40.190 --> 01:07:43.130
You guys made the choice and it again,

01:07:43.130 --> 01:07:47.430
it's like no one's said
that out loud to us but--

01:07:47.430 --> 01:07:50.402
Oh, I've seen people say it.

01:07:50.402 --> 01:07:51.880
They've typed it maybe.

01:07:51.880 --> 01:07:53.130
I've seen it typed.

01:07:53.130 --> 01:07:56.230
I saw it typed actually
after our first two episodes.

01:07:56.230 --> 01:07:57.927
Somebody was like "What's the big deal?

01:07:57.927 --> 01:07:59.007
"It's clear what happened.

01:07:59.007 --> 01:08:00.217
"They went to Los Angeles

01:08:00.217 --> 01:08:01.570
"and they lost their faith."

01:08:01.570 --> 01:08:02.503
It happens.

01:08:03.400 --> 01:08:06.300
And I'm just trying to
first of all hopefully,

01:08:06.300 --> 01:08:07.580
if you've listened to this point,

01:08:07.580 --> 01:08:11.120
you at least acknowledge
that this was a process

01:08:11.120 --> 01:08:14.150
that was in many ways
independent of where I was at

01:08:15.890 --> 01:08:19.453
but also way more personal and torturous

01:08:19.453 --> 01:08:24.260
and it wasn't a calculated
business decision.

01:08:24.260 --> 01:08:27.820
It wasn't like I don't know,

01:08:27.820 --> 01:08:31.020
that particular accusation hurts a lot.

01:08:31.020 --> 01:08:32.720
When people say you were never a Christian

01:08:32.720 --> 01:08:35.260
and what people say you
changed because of L.A.,

01:08:35.260 --> 01:08:39.570
those things hurt a lot
because of how untrue

01:08:39.570 --> 01:08:40.680
I know them to be.

01:08:40.680 --> 01:08:42.980
So there's an aspect, and I
will get into more of this.

01:08:42.980 --> 01:08:43.813
Okay.

01:08:43.813 --> 01:08:44.700
So I think we'll come back to it

01:08:44.700 --> 01:08:47.930
but your point for now is that

01:08:47.930 --> 01:08:51.970
there was an aspect of you
changing because of L.A.

01:08:51.970 --> 01:08:54.393
Yeah and this is where
L.A. comes into play.

01:08:55.550 --> 01:08:58.670
L.A. did allow me to ask a new question

01:08:58.670 --> 01:09:00.983
and that was why am I still doing this?

01:09:02.190 --> 01:09:04.290
And I'll be honest, I would
not have asked that question

01:09:04.290 --> 01:09:05.290
if I was in North Carolina

01:09:05.290 --> 01:09:06.960
because when you're in the Bible Belt,

01:09:06.960 --> 01:09:08.850
you're embedded in Christian culture.

01:09:08.850 --> 01:09:10.550
There are a dozens of reasons

01:09:10.550 --> 01:09:11.810
why you would still be doing it.

01:09:11.810 --> 01:09:14.250
I mean why rock the boat?

01:09:14.250 --> 01:09:16.300
Why disappoint your parents?

01:09:16.300 --> 01:09:18.400
Why disappoint your friends?

01:09:18.400 --> 01:09:21.740
Why extra you know get yourself
out of this and community.

01:09:21.740 --> 01:09:23.940
I would have been going to the same church

01:09:24.890 --> 01:09:27.040
since I was in ninth grade.

01:09:27.040 --> 01:09:28.580
I would say technically your whole life

01:09:28.580 --> 01:09:30.530
because that church
came from another church

01:09:30.530 --> 01:09:31.740
that we both went to.
Right.

01:09:31.740 --> 01:09:32.573
Exactly.

01:09:32.573 --> 01:09:34.820
I've been with the same
group of believers forever

01:09:34.820 --> 01:09:36.270
and now I was leading a Bible study.

01:09:36.270 --> 01:09:39.592
I had preached sermons on
Sunday you know what I'm saying?

01:09:39.592 --> 01:09:42.750
There's all kinds of reasons not to leave.

01:09:42.750 --> 01:09:45.500
Why damage your reputation
because honestly,

01:09:45.500 --> 01:09:49.590
in the Bible Belt this can
be as many people know,

01:09:49.590 --> 01:09:51.580
if you've left the faith
and the Bible Belt.

01:09:51.580 --> 01:09:52.930
It ain't easy.

01:09:52.930 --> 01:09:56.259
There's a lot of pressure to
stick around and stay in there.

01:09:56.259 --> 01:09:59.590
But what I realize is that I've
been pulling on this thread

01:09:59.590 --> 01:10:01.780
for a really long time, right?

01:10:01.780 --> 01:10:03.270
Let's call it the sweater of faith

01:10:03.270 --> 01:10:05.112
which is not the armor of God.

01:10:05.112 --> 01:10:07.810
This is a real offline concept.

01:10:07.810 --> 01:10:09.480
The sweater of faith.

01:10:09.480 --> 01:10:12.085
I've been pulling on this thread

01:10:12.085 --> 01:10:14.520
and it had sort of like turned into a vest

01:10:15.690 --> 01:10:19.104
and then a midriff and then a halter top

01:10:19.104 --> 01:10:21.960
and now it was a string bikini.

01:10:21.960 --> 01:10:23.860
It's not appropriate.

01:10:23.860 --> 01:10:27.340
And I was like I'm gonna
take the bikini off.

01:10:27.340 --> 01:10:28.740
Really not appropriate.

01:10:28.740 --> 01:10:29.720
It's just an analogy.

01:10:29.720 --> 01:10:30.660
Okay.

01:10:30.660 --> 01:10:32.090
And I was L.A.

01:10:32.090 --> 01:10:32.923
Yeah.

01:10:32.923 --> 01:10:36.150
Men in bikini tops, there's
lots place you can see--

01:10:36.150 --> 01:10:39.163
Go to the convenience store.

01:10:39.997 --> 01:10:44.770
And I took it off and I call this--

01:10:44.770 --> 01:10:47.440
What do you mean, how did you take it off?

01:10:47.440 --> 01:10:48.862
Well I have a journal entry, thankfully.

01:10:48.862 --> 01:10:50.360
That's great, okay.

01:10:50.360 --> 01:10:51.193
Give it to me.

01:10:51.193 --> 01:10:52.760
It has nothing to do with bikinis.

01:10:54.890 --> 01:10:57.443
This is from 2014, okay.

01:10:58.767 --> 01:11:01.267
"I understand that it is unreasonable

01:11:01.267 --> 01:11:03.327
"to expect Christianity to be a set

01:11:03.327 --> 01:11:06.177
"of scientifically verifiable principles.

01:11:06.177 --> 01:11:09.597
"It is a faith implying
that some sort of believing

01:11:09.597 --> 01:11:11.213
"without seeing is involved.

01:11:11.213 --> 01:11:14.037
"And more specifically, Christianity

01:11:14.037 --> 01:11:16.137
"is a relationship with Jesus

01:11:16.137 --> 01:11:18.377
"and relationships are not well defined

01:11:18.377 --> 01:11:20.745
"or experienced scientifically.

01:11:20.745 --> 01:11:24.297
"However, I don't think it insignificant

01:11:24.297 --> 01:11:28.237
"that the deeper I have
dug into Christianity

01:11:28.237 --> 01:11:30.487
"with a thirst for the truth,

01:11:30.487 --> 01:11:32.677
"the more difficult it
has become to have faith.

01:11:32.677 --> 01:11:35.887
"In fact, for me, it
has become impossible."

01:11:38.140 --> 01:11:40.492
And that was kind of the
reckoning for me, right?

01:11:40.492 --> 01:11:45.330
That was that was jumping
ship to use a better analogy

01:11:45.330 --> 01:11:47.570
than taking off a bikini.

01:11:47.570 --> 01:11:51.502
You see, I kind of saw
Christianity as this boat

01:11:51.502 --> 01:11:53.623
in a very stormy sea.

01:11:54.660 --> 01:11:56.600
It's stable, there's a
lot of other people on it,

01:11:56.600 --> 01:11:59.380
It's got a destination,
you're gonna get through this.

01:11:59.380 --> 01:12:01.690
It gives you something to hold on to.

01:12:01.690 --> 01:12:03.272
It gives you stability,
it gives you purpose,

01:12:03.272 --> 01:12:05.973
it gives you direction and
it gives you community.

01:12:07.530 --> 01:12:12.363
And when I jumped ship, I
didn't jump to another boat.

01:12:13.410 --> 01:12:17.807
I jumped into the water
and I pulled my wife

01:12:17.807 --> 01:12:19.703
and my children in with me.

01:12:22.530 --> 01:12:25.500
I jumped into a sea of uncertainty

01:12:28.034 --> 01:12:32.433
and that's where I've
lived for about six years.

01:12:35.560 --> 01:12:38.190
And we're gonna spend some
time talking a little bit more

01:12:38.190 --> 01:12:39.350
about where we're at now.

01:12:39.350 --> 01:12:41.610
I do wanna talk about it now
but we're getting more detail

01:12:41.610 --> 01:12:44.600
and like a subsequent podcast,
maybe in a Q&amp;A or something

01:12:44.600 --> 01:12:46.280
but I wanna kind of talk

01:12:46.280 --> 01:12:47.920
about what this has been like

01:12:47.920 --> 01:12:49.210
without getting into too much detail

01:12:49.210 --> 01:12:50.920
and I know because we're
already pretty long.

01:12:50.920 --> 01:12:52.320
This is gonna be a long one.

01:12:55.140 --> 01:12:57.671
Right after I jumped ship,

01:12:57.671 --> 01:13:01.893
I kind of went through a period of anger.

01:13:03.680 --> 01:13:08.680
I was very mad at the
Christian leaders and thinkers

01:13:10.350 --> 01:13:12.140
who I felt deceived by.

01:13:12.140 --> 01:13:14.600
I wanna be very clear about this.

01:13:14.600 --> 01:13:17.714
No one that I was in
personal contact with,

01:13:17.714 --> 01:13:22.714
pastors, Christian friends,
elders in my church,

01:13:23.320 --> 01:13:25.640
none of them disappointed
me or let me down.

01:13:25.640 --> 01:13:28.550
I did not have a personal like tragedy.

01:13:28.550 --> 01:13:29.383
A lot of people have like

01:13:29.383 --> 01:13:31.720
a traumatic spiritual
experience in a church.

01:13:31.720 --> 01:13:32.840
I didn't.

01:13:32.840 --> 01:13:35.210
I only got good things from the church.

01:13:35.210 --> 01:13:37.606
We talked about this while
back that like listen,

01:13:37.606 --> 01:13:40.023
I'm a straight white dude.

01:13:41.630 --> 01:13:43.760
You know you get a lot
of things handed to you

01:13:43.760 --> 01:13:47.300
especially within the church
if you fit that profile.

01:13:47.300 --> 01:13:50.660
In some churches, being a straight dude

01:13:51.736 --> 01:13:54.930
is the only way that you can teach.

01:13:54.930 --> 01:13:56.910
There's plenty of churches right now,

01:13:56.910 --> 01:13:58.550
churches in Los Angeles

01:13:58.550 --> 01:14:00.960
that people would consider progressive

01:14:00.960 --> 01:14:03.830
where you better not tell them you're gay

01:14:04.700 --> 01:14:07.700
and if you're a woman, you
probably won't be able to preach.

01:14:08.800 --> 01:14:10.683
It's 2020 and this is still the case.

01:14:10.683 --> 01:14:12.120
I just wanna be clear about that.

01:14:12.120 --> 01:14:17.120
But for me, this had been
I got so much out of this.

01:14:17.310 --> 01:14:18.670
I was riding high.

01:14:18.670 --> 01:14:21.150
I could have ridden this
train to the top man,

01:14:21.150 --> 01:14:22.393
you know what I'm saying?

01:14:24.187 --> 01:14:27.520
But nobody disappointed me personally

01:14:27.520 --> 01:14:30.730
but I was angry at the thinkers.

01:14:30.730 --> 01:14:32.630
I was angry at the people
who had written the book

01:14:32.630 --> 01:14:34.420
saying that evolution
didn't have any evidence.

01:14:34.420 --> 01:14:36.570
I was angry at the people

01:14:36.570 --> 01:14:38.500
who had written systematic theology books

01:14:38.500 --> 01:14:41.650
who basically made it seem like
this was all pretty simple.

01:14:41.650 --> 01:14:46.250
And I kind of, the pendulum
swung for a time into atheism.

01:14:46.250 --> 01:14:48.070
I was like this is all bullshit

01:14:48.070 --> 01:14:51.530
and I'm gonna be the enemy of this stuff.

01:14:51.530 --> 01:14:54.260
I'm gonna be an anti evangelist.

01:14:54.260 --> 01:14:55.570
That's what I was thinking at the time.

01:14:55.570 --> 01:14:58.100
Of course, we're still
very private about all this

01:14:58.100 --> 01:15:01.090
so it wasn't like I said
this to anybody publicly.

01:15:01.090 --> 01:15:06.090
And that anger actually
subsided rather quickly.

01:15:06.380 --> 01:15:07.213
It's interesting.

01:15:07.213 --> 01:15:11.220
I kind of had my moment
of anger in atheism

01:15:12.800 --> 01:15:17.340
and then that was replaced with

01:15:17.340 --> 01:15:20.210
kind of an openness and a curiosity.

01:15:20.210 --> 01:15:24.590
You know it's interesting how liberating

01:15:24.590 --> 01:15:25.990
this one aspect has been.

01:15:25.990 --> 01:15:27.250
I think the biggest change

01:15:27.250 --> 01:15:29.680
that has happened to me in my life

01:15:29.680 --> 01:15:32.720
is that I've lost my
appetite for certainty,

01:15:32.720 --> 01:15:34.740
specifically certainty about things

01:15:34.740 --> 01:15:37.000
I don't think you can be certain about.

01:15:37.000 --> 01:15:40.430
I think my struggle with Christianity

01:15:40.430 --> 01:15:42.071
for me a big part of it was

01:15:42.071 --> 01:15:45.040
I had to keep aligning my
thoughts and being certain

01:15:45.040 --> 01:15:46.667
and kind of reader living my faith

01:15:46.667 --> 01:15:49.030
and why this was reasonable
and being sure about this

01:15:49.030 --> 01:15:50.437
and knowing exactly what
was gonna happen when I died

01:15:50.437 --> 01:15:52.060
and all this stuff.

01:15:52.060 --> 01:15:53.150
But when I was like

01:15:53.150 --> 01:15:54.810
I don't think I can be
certain about these things,

01:15:54.810 --> 01:15:56.880
it's like when a person
I've heard this happens,

01:15:56.880 --> 01:15:58.230
I haven't done it yet.

01:15:58.230 --> 01:16:00.660
When you stop eating meat, you
lose your appetite for meat,

01:16:00.660 --> 01:16:01.660
a lot of people say.

01:16:02.720 --> 01:16:04.459
I stopped being certain about things.

01:16:04.459 --> 01:16:06.430
I lost my appetite to be certain.

01:16:06.430 --> 01:16:08.450
I didn't wake up with a sense of panic.

01:16:08.450 --> 01:16:09.870
I thought there would be panic,

01:16:09.870 --> 01:16:11.440
I thought there would be chaos

01:16:12.960 --> 01:16:15.877
Especially for someone who
that's how you lived your life.

01:16:15.877 --> 01:16:16.797
And I thought there would be few.

01:16:16.797 --> 01:16:18.680
And so attached to it.

01:16:18.680 --> 01:16:19.590
Right.

01:16:19.590 --> 01:16:22.360
But it's been the most liberating thing

01:16:22.360 --> 01:16:24.110
that has happened in my adult life.

01:16:24.110 --> 01:16:25.540
I'm not kidding.

01:16:25.540 --> 01:16:26.450
I'm not trying to paint that,

01:16:26.450 --> 01:16:28.720
listen, it's not like I'm about
to give you some philosophy

01:16:28.720 --> 01:16:29.970
that I live according to now

01:16:29.970 --> 01:16:31.460
that's got did the gives

01:16:31.460 --> 01:16:33.310
that gives me community
purpose and meaning.

01:16:33.310 --> 01:16:34.573
I don't have that, okay.

01:16:36.360 --> 01:16:38.490
I think there's a giant sort of shift

01:16:38.490 --> 01:16:39.700
that's happening culturally

01:16:39.700 --> 01:16:42.430
and I think that we may be
arriving at that some time.

01:16:42.430 --> 01:16:44.229
But it doesn't exist right now for me.

01:16:44.229 --> 01:16:48.920
But what does exist is an
openness, is this curiosity.

01:16:48.920 --> 01:16:53.920
Listen, I still think that
belief in God is very reasonable.

01:16:54.553 --> 01:16:57.130
I think that the idea that the universe

01:16:57.130 --> 01:16:58.880
is ultimately purposeful,

01:16:58.880 --> 01:17:01.470
it's headed towards some ultimate purpose,

01:17:01.470 --> 01:17:04.200
not only is that comforting
but it kind of feels

01:17:04.200 --> 01:17:06.580
again, it feels right
to me when I just look

01:17:06.580 --> 01:17:10.850
at the history of the
world and we're you know.

01:17:10.850 --> 01:17:13.060
But I don't know it to be certain

01:17:13.060 --> 01:17:16.250
and I don't know anything
about this source or this god

01:17:16.250 --> 01:17:18.210
that might be behind all this

01:17:18.210 --> 01:17:21.005
and I'm kind of beginning to think that

01:17:21.005 --> 01:17:22.980
I don't know if you are supposed

01:17:22.980 --> 01:17:24.430
to know a whole lot about it.

01:17:26.220 --> 01:17:29.860
So I would call myself a hopeful agnostic

01:17:29.860 --> 01:17:33.860
meaning I don't know, but I hope.

01:17:33.860 --> 01:17:35.900
I hope there's something.

01:17:35.900 --> 01:17:37.840
A question that I've
gotten from some people

01:17:37.840 --> 01:17:40.130
who are close to me, love me

01:17:40.130 --> 01:17:42.563
is what do you think
happens after you die?

01:17:45.330 --> 01:17:46.163
I don't know.

01:17:47.000 --> 01:17:49.920
I'm reasonably certain
that you don't burn in hell

01:17:49.920 --> 01:17:52.900
because you were intellectually
curious and honest

01:17:52.900 --> 01:17:53.803
to put it bluntly.

01:17:55.062 --> 01:17:59.620
But honestly, I'm more interested now

01:17:59.620 --> 01:18:01.283
in what happens while I live.

01:18:02.870 --> 01:18:04.730
It's not so much what
happens after you die

01:18:04.730 --> 01:18:07.113
but what happens while you're alive.

01:18:09.850 --> 01:18:12.069
And I'm trying to answer that question

01:18:12.069 --> 01:18:14.803
but it's one of the
reasons I'm in therapy.

01:18:16.190 --> 01:18:20.040
It's honestly one of the reasons
that I get up every morning

01:18:20.040 --> 01:18:22.610
and do 20 minutes of back exercises.

01:18:22.610 --> 01:18:26.260
Honestly, it's one of the reasons

01:18:26.260 --> 01:18:28.790
that I think more about what I eat

01:18:32.000 --> 01:18:35.613
because the only thing I know
that I've got is this life.

01:18:35.613 --> 01:18:37.860
But the other thing that
has kind of happened

01:18:37.860 --> 01:18:41.130
because people ask me about
your marriage, your kids,

01:18:41.130 --> 01:18:43.310
will get into this in more detail.

01:18:43.310 --> 01:18:47.860
But Jesse has her own story,
there's been a lot of crying

01:18:50.290 --> 01:18:53.290
but she's in a similar place now

01:18:54.400 --> 01:18:57.940
and this process because we were so,

01:18:57.940 --> 01:19:00.400
this whole process ruins
a lot of marriages.

01:19:00.400 --> 01:19:03.790
I've seen it a lot
because sometimes people

01:19:03.790 --> 01:19:04.670
are like I can't go .

01:19:04.670 --> 01:19:06.660
They're not going there, it's over.

01:19:06.660 --> 01:19:07.810
This was the whole foundation.

01:19:07.810 --> 01:19:09.470
I mean yeah we made vows.

01:19:09.470 --> 01:19:12.060
If you read, we wrote our
own vows for our wedding

01:19:12.060 --> 01:19:13.760
and they were very much about--

01:19:13.760 --> 01:19:14.593
Jesus

01:19:14.593 --> 01:19:15.426
Jesus.

01:19:17.135 --> 01:19:19.440
But now, it's kind of like our marriage

01:19:19.440 --> 01:19:20.820
has hit a second wind

01:19:22.230 --> 01:19:27.070
where it's not so much about a structure

01:19:27.070 --> 01:19:29.130
that we both sort of assent to

01:19:29.130 --> 01:19:31.720
that tells us what our
marriage should be like

01:19:31.720 --> 01:19:34.910
but it's like hey, it's pretty cool

01:19:34.910 --> 01:19:36.860
that I get to go through life with you.

01:19:37.820 --> 01:19:38.653
I love you.

01:19:40.400 --> 01:19:41.648
And that has actually been

01:19:41.648 --> 01:19:44.343
a pretty good thing to concentrate on.

01:19:47.614 --> 01:19:51.607
And with the kids, you know
I think for me the idea

01:19:52.845 --> 01:19:54.930
that the purpose and meaning

01:19:54.930 --> 01:19:58.040
and sort of like orienting
your life in a certain way,

01:19:58.040 --> 01:20:02.133
all came from the Bible and from church.

01:20:03.617 --> 01:20:07.030
I actually because none of that went away,

01:20:07.030 --> 01:20:11.470
you know I'm saying, like I still

01:20:11.470 --> 01:20:13.649
wanna be the same kind of person

01:20:13.649 --> 01:20:15.020
that I've always wanted to be.

01:20:15.020 --> 01:20:16.210
I wanna be the same kind of husband.

01:20:16.210 --> 01:20:18.560
I want the best for my kids.

01:20:18.560 --> 01:20:20.500
Meaning like your morality?

01:20:20.500 --> 01:20:21.333
Yeah

01:20:21.333 --> 01:20:22.200
Still like you--

01:20:22.200 --> 01:20:23.033
Yeah.
You know what?

01:20:23.033 --> 01:20:25.770
The moment that you jumped ship,

01:20:25.770 --> 01:20:28.260
you didn't start looking
to cheat on your wife.

01:20:28.260 --> 01:20:29.093
Right.

01:20:29.093 --> 01:20:30.530
As an example.
Exactly.

01:20:30.530 --> 01:20:32.040
It wasn't like all of a sudden 'cause

01:20:32.040 --> 01:20:32.927
I'd always been told that

01:20:32.927 --> 01:20:35.250
and I had many Christians who I respected

01:20:35.250 --> 01:20:38.497
said "Man, if God wasn't real,

01:20:38.497 --> 01:20:41.417
"I would be out doing drugs right now,

01:20:41.417 --> 01:20:43.700
"I'd be out sleeping with whoever I want."

01:20:43.700 --> 01:20:47.580
I'm like I don't actually think you would.

01:20:47.580 --> 01:20:50.450
I think you actually have an innate desire

01:20:50.450 --> 01:20:52.260
to be a pretty good person

01:20:52.260 --> 01:20:54.750
and to live a life that is good for you

01:20:54.750 --> 01:20:56.680
and the people you love.

01:20:56.680 --> 01:21:00.160
And a lot of people will
attach it to a structure

01:21:00.160 --> 01:21:02.240
and an explanation like Christianity.

01:21:02.240 --> 01:21:04.743
But I think very few people actually

01:21:04.743 --> 01:21:08.130
find the purpose in their faith.

01:21:08.130 --> 01:21:09.880
I think they have purpose

01:21:09.880 --> 01:21:11.630
and then they bolster it with faith.

01:21:11.630 --> 01:21:13.060
That's my personal opinion.

01:21:13.060 --> 01:21:14.760
Or even another way to put it

01:21:14.760 --> 01:21:18.111
using the marriage example,

01:21:18.111 --> 01:21:23.111
do you think that your
motive to be true to Jesse

01:21:24.237 --> 01:21:27.270
was not just out of love for her

01:21:27.270 --> 01:21:30.230
but out of love for God you know,

01:21:30.230 --> 01:21:32.860
out of respect for you know.

01:21:32.860 --> 01:21:37.780
So now you being true to
Jesse is out of love for her.

01:21:37.780 --> 01:21:40.320
It's a line like I'm--

01:21:40.320 --> 01:21:45.320
Yeah and it's not a fear of God.

01:21:50.231 --> 01:21:51.560
It's a love for her

01:21:51.560 --> 01:21:52.963
and it's a fear of listen,

01:21:53.878 --> 01:21:55.680
there's a lot of shit that happens

01:21:55.680 --> 01:21:57.800
when you do stuff like that in your life.

01:21:57.800 --> 01:22:01.190
There are natural built-in consequences

01:22:01.190 --> 01:22:03.600
to doing the things that are traditionally

01:22:03.600 --> 01:22:05.670
considered to be sinful

01:22:05.670 --> 01:22:08.210
according to every religious tradition.

01:22:08.210 --> 01:22:09.410
It's not like you just...

01:22:09.410 --> 01:22:11.250
If I didn't have this I'd be out

01:22:11.250 --> 01:22:13.286
doing all kinds of crazy shit.

01:22:13.286 --> 01:22:15.020
No, you wouldn't.

01:22:15.020 --> 01:22:20.020
It's like first of all,
my best friends now

01:22:20.281 --> 01:22:25.281
are not Christians but they're faithful

01:22:27.160 --> 01:22:28.630
to their families and--

01:22:28.630 --> 01:22:29.463
They're not horrible people.

01:22:29.463 --> 01:22:30.550
They're not horrible people.

01:22:30.550 --> 01:22:32.440
And I think that's what we thought

01:22:32.440 --> 01:22:37.440
was without the Holy
Spirit indwelling you,

01:22:38.693 --> 01:22:43.693
you're just going off
the flesh so to speak,

01:22:44.010 --> 01:22:45.610
you're going off of your own desires

01:22:45.610 --> 01:22:47.930
and I mean that's the
only thing keeping you

01:22:47.930 --> 01:22:49.140
from being a horrible person.

01:22:49.140 --> 01:22:50.380
I think that's from a young age,

01:22:50.380 --> 01:22:51.790
I think that's what we felt.

01:22:51.790 --> 01:22:53.027
But I think the thing you

01:22:53.027 --> 01:22:55.170
That's a particular view of people

01:22:55.170 --> 01:22:56.700
that we had in our particular

01:22:56.700 --> 01:23:00.750
like reformed Calvinistic.

01:23:00.750 --> 01:23:02.637
Everyone is totally braved.
Yeah, it's--

01:23:02.637 --> 01:23:04.800
And anything good that
is coming from anybody

01:23:04.800 --> 01:23:07.130
is either because they are
created in the image of God

01:23:07.130 --> 01:23:09.070
or they have a relationship with God.

01:23:09.070 --> 01:23:10.810
I think too, I wanna get back

01:23:10.810 --> 01:23:13.120
to like that being a
subsection and everything

01:23:13.120 --> 01:23:17.360
that you've talked about being applied

01:23:17.360 --> 01:23:20.940
to the whole of Christianity
or faith or anything like that.

01:23:20.940 --> 01:23:23.780
But before that, you were talking about

01:23:23.780 --> 01:23:26.420
you were moving to the kids

01:23:26.420 --> 01:23:27.860
from your relationship with Jesse.

01:23:27.860 --> 01:23:29.560
I kind of went back to the
relationship with Jesse.

01:23:29.560 --> 01:23:30.660
So when you were talking about the kids,

01:23:30.660 --> 01:23:35.080
you were talking about
raising them in a way

01:23:35.080 --> 01:23:40.080
to be whole people, to be good people.

01:23:42.950 --> 01:23:44.570
I don't wanna put words in your mouth

01:23:44.570 --> 01:23:45.460
but I think you were getting it.

01:23:45.460 --> 01:23:48.890
Well, I think the biggest thing about kids

01:23:48.890 --> 01:23:51.810
is what I have sort of observed

01:23:51.810 --> 01:23:54.210
and being very much embedded in the church

01:23:54.210 --> 01:23:55.800
for a very long time

01:23:58.010 --> 01:24:00.140
is there's kind of this idea

01:24:00.140 --> 01:24:04.250
that it is your responsibility as parents

01:24:04.250 --> 01:24:06.380
to make sure your kids turn out all right

01:24:06.380 --> 01:24:07.640
and that it's up to you,

01:24:07.640 --> 01:24:08.930
you better teach them the right thing.

01:24:08.930 --> 01:24:11.483
If you don't, they're gonna be screwed up.

01:24:13.008 --> 01:24:17.500
And I'm not saying that

01:24:17.500 --> 01:24:20.010
you shouldn't teach your kids good things.

01:24:20.010 --> 01:24:23.490
But what I've observed
is that you know what

01:24:23.490 --> 01:24:25.390
my kids could actually teach me a lot.

01:24:27.161 --> 01:24:32.161
I think that kids orient themselves

01:24:33.100 --> 01:24:37.717
in the world much more
readily based on your behavior

01:24:37.717 --> 01:24:40.043
than the specific things
that you tell them.

01:24:41.720 --> 01:24:42.870
I don't think that having

01:24:42.870 --> 01:24:46.541
an information session with your kids

01:24:46.541 --> 01:24:48.600
and indoctrinating them

01:24:48.600 --> 01:24:52.020
it's what's going to make
them into a good person.

01:24:52.020 --> 01:24:53.880
I'm not saying we're
not constantly talking

01:24:53.880 --> 01:24:55.870
about issues of morality

01:24:55.870 --> 01:24:58.720
and ethical things, philosophical things.

01:24:58.720 --> 01:25:00.140
We talk about that every time,

01:25:00.140 --> 01:25:04.313
our family is very much always
talking about these things.

01:25:05.778 --> 01:25:08.120
But the interesting the
sort of freeing thing

01:25:08.120 --> 01:25:11.763
is is that when my kids
have a question about God

01:25:11.763 --> 01:25:15.880
or the deeper purpose of the universe

01:25:15.880 --> 01:25:17.460
or what happens when you die,

01:25:17.460 --> 01:25:19.650
we explore those things as people.

01:25:19.650 --> 01:25:21.350
I'm not here as some authority

01:25:21.350 --> 01:25:23.740
that's gonna point you
to this ironclad thing

01:25:23.740 --> 01:25:24.900
and that's gonna make it okay

01:25:24.900 --> 01:25:28.000
because you know what, it's
not gonna make it okay.

01:25:28.000 --> 01:25:29.650
Just because I can point to this book

01:25:29.650 --> 01:25:30.956
and tell you that you should believe this

01:25:30.956 --> 01:25:35.560
